      "explanation": "Vietnamese extended family maintains an absolute structural division between **BÊN NỘI (Paternal / 'Inside' Clan)** and **BÊN NGOẠI (Maternal / 'Outside' Clan)**.\n\n1. **Grandparents (Ông Bà):**\n- **Paternal Side (Bên Nội - Father's parents):**\n  * **ông nội** [OHNG NOY / oŋ˧˧ noj˧˨ʔ] — Paternal Grandfather\n  * **bà nội** [BAH NOY / ɓaː˨˩ noj˧˨ʔ] — Paternal Grandmother\n- **Maternal Side (Bên Ngoại - Mother's parents):**\n  * **ông ngoại** [OHNG NGWY / oŋ˧˧ ŋwaːj˧˨ʔ] — Maternal Grandfather\n  * **bà ngoại** [BAH NGWY / ɓaː˨˩ ŋwaːj˧˨ʔ] — Maternal Grandmother\n\n2. **Uncles & Aunts (5 Distinct Specific Kinship Terms!):**\n- **bác** [BAHK] — Older uncle or aunt (older sibling of EITHER father or mother)\n- **chú** [CHOO] — Father's **younger brother**\n- **cô** [KOH] — Father's **sister** (younger or older)\n- **cậu** [KOW] — Mother's **younger brother**\n- **dì** [ZEE / yee] — Mother's **younger sister**\n\n3. **Cousins & Grandchildren / Nieces / Nephews:**\n- **anh chị em họ** [ahng chee ehm HAW] — Cousins\n- **cháu** [CHOW] — Grandchild OR Niece / Nephew (one word covers the generation below!).",
