    "objective": "Identify and classify staple Vietnamese food, noodle dishes, meats, and street beverages.",
    "presentation": {
      "explanation": "Vietnamese cuisine (*ẩm thực Việt Nam*) is renowned for its fresh herbs, clear broths, and street food culture:\n\n1. Food Staples & Signature Dishes:\n   - cơm (cooked rice): cơm tấm (broken rice with grilled pork chop), cơm gà (chicken rice)\n   - phở (flat rice noodle soup with aromatic beef/chicken broth: phở bò, phở gà)\n   - bún (round rice noodles: bún chả = grilled pork with noodles, bún bò Huế = spicy beef noodles)\n   - bánh mì (Vietnamese crispy baguette stuffed with pâté, cold cuts, pickled daikon/carrots, and cilantro)\n   - thịt (meat): thịt bò (beef), thịt gà (chicken), thịt heo / thịt lợn (pork — heo in South, lợn in North)\n   - cá (fish), tôm (shrimp), hải sản (seafood)\n   - rau (vegetables / fresh greens)\n   - trứng (egg: trứng ốp la = fried sunny-side egg)\n\n2. Iconic Beverages (Đồ uống):\n   - cà phê sữa đá (Vietnamese iced milk coffee with sweetened condensed milk)\n   - cà phê đen đá (iced black coffee)\n   - trà đá (iced tea — omnipresent at every street stall)\n   - nước dừa (fresh coconut water)\n   - sinh tố (fresh fruit smoothie: sinh tố bơ = avocado smoothie)",
      "examples": [
        {
          "target": "Cho tôi một bát phở bò tái và một cốc trà đá.",
          "reading": "chaw toy moht baht fuh baw tye vah moht cawk chrah dah.",
          "translation": "Give me a bowl of medium-rare beef pho and a glass of iced tea."
        },
        {
          "target": "Buổi sáng tôi thường ăn bánh mì kẹp thịt.",
          "reading": "bwoy sahng toy teo-eng ahn bahn mee kehp teet.",
          "translation": "In the morning I usually eat a meat-stuffed baguette."
        },
        {
          "target": "Cà phê sữa đá Việt Nam rất đậm đà và thơm ngon.",
          "reading": "kah feh sew-ah dah vee-et nahm zaht duh-m dah vah tuhm ngawn.",
          "translation": "Vietnamese iced milk coffee is very rich, robust, and delicious."
        },
        {
          "target": "Ở Sài Gòn, cơm tấm sườn nướng rất nổi tiếng.",
          "reading": "uh sigh gawn, kuhm tuhm sew-on new-awng zaht noy tee-eng.",
          "translation": "In Saigon, broken rice with grilled ribs is very famous."
        }
      ],
      "mnemonics": [
        "Phở bò = beef pho; Phở gà = chicken pho (gà = 'cluck like a chicken').",
        "Trà đá = iced tea (đá = ice / stone / rock cold!).",
        "Cơm tấm = broken rice (tấm = broken grain)."
      ],
      "culturalNotes": [
        "Drinking *trà đá* (iced tea) on small blue plastic chairs on the sidewalk (*vỉa hè*) while watching the street traffic is the most universal social activity across all regions in Vietnam."
      ]
    },
